Static instances of ndexr.io's own Inter (src/vendor/fonts/InterVariable.woff2),
plus JetBrains Mono 2.304 for code (JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf from
JetBrainsMono-2.304.zip, sha256 6f6376c6…, the source Inlet 0012 ships):
the Regolith look. egui reads TTF and draws a variable font only at its default
instance, hence fixed weights here.
Regenerate Inter with fontTools: instancer.instantiateVariableFont(..., {"wght": N}).
Inter: SIL OFL 1.1. JetBrains Mono: SIL OFL 1.1.

Symbol fallbacks (2026-10-18), last in every family so they only fill gaps:
DejaVuSans-symbols.ttf and NotoSansSymbols2-symbols.ttf, cut from the system's
DejaVuSans.ttf and NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf with fontTools (stack env
env/r4.6_py3.13-release):
  python3 -m fontTools.subset <font> --no-hinting --layout-features='' \
    --unicodes=U+2190-21FF,U+2300-23FF,U+2500-25FF,U+2600-27BF,U+27F0-27FF,U+2900-297F,U+2B00-2BFF,U+FF01-FF5E
DejaVu: Bitstream Vera / public-domain changes. Noto Sans Symbols 2: SIL OFL 1.1.
theme.rs `every_symbol_in_the_ui_has_a_glyph` fails on any UI symbol none of them draws.

Licence texts: LICENSE-OFL.txt (Inter, JetBrains Mono, Noto Sans Symbols 2)
and LICENSE-DejaVu.txt (DejaVu), shipped beside the fonts as their licences ask.
